From: Michael Podolszki <m.podolszki@phytec.de>
Date: Tue, 9 Sep 2026 12:15:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/imx: dpu95: stop shouting about descriptors userspace got
 wrong

With weston on the g2d renderer (weston.ini: use-g2d=true, libg2d-dpu.so.2.4.0
mapped into the process), the i.MX95 DPU floods the kernel log at every
repaint:

  imx95-dpu 4b400000.display-controller: [drm] *ERROR* failed to get dmabuf

Every blit that sets use_dma_fd goes through dpu95_be_get_plane_addr(), which
walks all three colour planes unconditionally and calls
dpu95_be_fd_to_address() for each source and destination descriptor. Whatever
libg2d puts in those slots is frequently not a dmabuf: instrumenting the error
path to print the descriptor and the errno gives fd 900, 438, 200 and 168, all
-EBADF, none of them open in the compositor. The values look like geometry,
not descriptors, so the library and this ioctl do not agree on the layout of
the buffer behind user_data. That is a userspace problem: the library is a
binary, the kernel already returns -EBADF to the caller, and the affected
planes carry no data -- the picture is correct either way.

What is a kernel problem is drm_err() on a path userspace can trigger once per
plane per frame. Demote both dma_buf_get() failures to drm_dbg(), so they stay
reachable via drm.debug but stop burying every other message in dmesg, and
name the descriptor and error so the log is worth reading when it is enabled.

Two related fixes in the same path:

 - Reject fd <= 0 before dma_buf_get(). The guard was "if (fd < 0)", but 0 is
   a valid descriptor -- the caller's stdin -- so a zeroed, unused plane slot
   reached dma_buf_get() and failed there. Treat it as "plane unused" and
   leave *phy alone.

 - The return value of dpu95_be_fd_to_address() was discarded and the plane
   offset added regardless. On a failed lookup with a non-zero offset that
   left src/dst_plane_addr[i] holding the bare offset, which is not an address
   at all, and dpu95_be_set_plane_addr() only tests for non-zero before
   programming it into the fetch and store units. Add the offset only when an
   address was actually obtained.

No functional change for well-formed requests: descriptors that resolved
before still resolve, and the addresses programmed into the DPU are the same.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Michael Podolszki <m.podolszki@phytec.de>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/imx/dpu95/dpu95-blit.c | 27 +++++++++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/imx/dpu95/dpu95-blit.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/imx/dpu95/dpu95-blit.c
@@ -274,12 +274,19 @@
 	struct sg_table *sgt = NULL;
 	struct dma_buf_attachment *attachment = NULL;
 
-	if (fd < 0)
-		return fd;
+	/*
+	 * Callers hand in one descriptor per colour plane and leave the planes
+	 * they do not use at 0 instead of -1. Zero is a perfectly valid file
+	 * descriptor (it is the caller's stdin), so it passed the original "< 0"
+	 * test and then failed dma_buf_get(). Treat it as "no plane" and return
+	 * without touching *phy, so the caller keeps its initial zero.
+	 */
+	if (fd <= 0)
+		return -ENOENT;
 
 	dmabuf = dma_buf_get(fd);
 	if (IS_ERR(dmabuf)) {
-		drm_err(drm_dev, "failed to get dmabuf\n");
+		drm_dbg(drm_dev, "fd %d is not a dmabuf: %pe\n", fd, dmabuf);
 		return PTR_ERR(dmabuf);
 	}
 	attachment = dma_buf_attach(dmabuf, drm_dev->dev);
@@ -311,12 +318,12 @@
 	int i;
 
 	for (i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
-		dpu95_be_fd_to_address(drm_dev,
-			plane_info.src_plane_fd[i], &src_plane_addr[i]);
-		src_plane_addr[i] += plane_info.src_plane_offset[i];
-		dpu95_be_fd_to_address(drm_dev,
-			plane_info.dst_plane_fd[i], &dst_plane_addr[i]);
-		dst_plane_addr[i] += plane_info.dst_plane_offset[i];
+		if (!dpu95_be_fd_to_address(drm_dev,
+				plane_info.src_plane_fd[i], &src_plane_addr[i]))
+			src_plane_addr[i] += plane_info.src_plane_offset[i];
+		if (!dpu95_be_fd_to_address(drm_dev,
+				plane_info.dst_plane_fd[i], &dst_plane_addr[i]))
+			dst_plane_addr[i] += plane_info.dst_plane_offset[i];
 	}
 }
 
@@ -689,7 +696,8 @@
 
 	dmabuf = dma_buf_get(flush->dmabuf_fd);
 	if (IS_ERR(dmabuf)) {
-		drm_err(drm_dev, "failed to get dmabuf\n");
+		drm_dbg(drm_dev, "sync: fd %d is not a dmabuf: %pe\n",
+			flush->dmabuf_fd, dmabuf);
 		return PTR_ERR(dmabuf);
 	}
 	attachment = dma_buf_attach(dmabuf, drm_dev->dev);
